extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 133-135 (cache p133-p135, page_offset 0). The class starts at the foot of printed 133, the abilities and skill lists are printed 134, equipment, money and cybernetics printed 135. Printed 134 checked against a 150 dpi render; OCR and render agree. No blood-rider class was in production on 2026-09-25. || RELATED LIST: the survey flagged printed 134 as a possible merged-columns page with no Physical / Pilot / Pilot Related lines. The render settles it: the book itself omits all three (and Horsemanship); the list runs Communications, Domestic, Electrical, Espionage, Mechanical, Medical, Military (none), Rogue, Science, Technical, W.P., Wilderness. Stored as printed - those categories are not offered. The Master Blood Rider (printed 136) prints Physical +5%, Pilot +5% and Pilot Related +5%, so the omission may be a book slip; recorded, not repaired. || XP: the Blood Rider / Blood Lizard ladder on printed 192, read off a render, as briefed. Level 11 prints 137,000 where level 10 ends - a book slip (every other band starts one above the previous band''s end) - stored AS PRINTED, 137000, per the brief; the strictly-rising rule still holds (96901 < 137000 < 188101). || GROUP: psychic - a major psionic whose occupation exists because of the psychic bond (the Psi-Slinger and Psi-Stalker precedent). The book files it under no group heading. No sdc_base or mdc_base is printed (the +3D6 S.D.C. is a pool bonus), so men_of_arms: true - a trained cavalry warrior, raider and scout with extreme physical training, as the Psi-Slinger and Psi-Stalker take the men-of-arms 3D6. || RACE: printed 133 calls Blood Riders human psychics; race_restrictions only none (the human case). The Achilles clans are still human riders. || PSIONICS: printed 134 says all Blood Riders are major psionics, select powers as appropriate (see Rifts RPG, page 12), determine I.S.P. as normal. Rifts RPG printed 12 (read from the text layer of Rifts Main): a major psionic selects eight powers from one of Sensitive, Physical or Healer, or six from any of the three; I.S.P. is M.E. + 4D6, +1D6+1 per level. The class psionics block carries the tier and that I.S.P. formula; the four choices are special_abilities behind a choose 1, each with its own count and category (the Felinoid shape), so categories union onto a class block that states none. That page also halves skill bonuses and related skills for a RANDOMLY ROLLED major psionic; not applied, since this is a psychic O.C.C. whose printed bonuses are its own. No new powers per level is printed. Master psionics (1%) use the Master Blood Rider class. || BONUSES: +1 P.S., +1 P.E., +1D6 Spd and +3D6 S.D.C. stored unconditionally. +1 strike and parry on lizard-back and the +3 saves while within 100 feet of the mount are conditional - special_abilities prose. || SKILLS: Language: Spanish 98; Literacy: Spanish (+15%) as Literacy: Native Language 40+15 (Spanish is the clans'' own tongue; the catalog has no Literacy: Spanish); Radio: Basic 45+10; Horsemanship (+15% to horses) as Horsemanship: General 40+15; Horsemanship: Exotic Animals stored at the general +15% (30+15), the +25% with Blood Lizards being conditional and in the note; Wilderness Survival 30+20; Tracking: Animals as Track & Trap Animals 20+15 (the catalog''s precedent for that printed name); Tracking: Humans as Tracking (people) 25+15; Land Navigation 36+10; W.P. Energy Rifle; one archaic W.P. as a choice among the catalog''s ancient W.P.s; one W.P. of choice; Hand to Hand: Expert, to Martial Arts or Assassin (evil) for one other skill each. || RELATED: 6, plus two at level 3 and one at 6, 8, 11 and 14. Communications any; Domestic +5; Electrical Basic Electronics only; Espionage Detect Ambush, Detect Concealment and Sniper only (+5%); Mechanical Automotive Mechanics only; Medical First Aid only; Rogue +5; Science Astronomy only (the catalog Astronomy row, not Astronomy & Navigation); Technical +10; W.P. any; Wilderness +10; Military none. Secondary: two at each of levels one, three and seven (count 2, schedule 3 and 7), the Sun Priest reading of this wording; same limits without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: Blood Rider Claw Armor (65 M.D.C.) is the catalog row; one energy weapon of choice and four E-clips; vibro-blade of choice; three archaic or non-energy weapons as a choose 3 from a catalog set; riding cloak as hooded-cloak (judgement); two traveling-clothes; fine clothes as dress-clothing. The saddle, the camping kit and the Blood Lizard mount itself have no catalog row and are not stubbed; the mount is the Blood Lizard R.C.C. || MONEY: 1D4x1000 credits. class-check warns that a race stating its own starting_money would discard it; race_restrictions only none means the class is never paired, so it always applies. Not supersedes_race."
---

## Lore

Blood Riders are human psychics from the ranching clans of the Silver River
plains, bonded mind to mind with Blood Lizards - fast, intelligent carnivorous
D-Bees that trust no one who is not a psychic. Through that bond they are the
finest cavalry on the continent, and skilled trackers, raiders and scouts.

Clan children are tested for psychic ability, and only about three in ten
qualify. The rest become ordinary horsemen or keep the lizards, while the gifted
spend their youth trying to forge a link with a mount; the attempt is dangerous,
and every clan loses an apprentice or two each year. A rider normally bonds with
a single lizard, since two bonded to one rider will fight each other jealously.

The clans ranch cattle and horses on their own lands, and sell riders'' services
as couriers, bodyguards and scouts, sharing the pay. In Santiago every clan
member belongs to the militia and rides patrol against the Larhold barbarians;
Cordoba persecutes them for keeping company with "demons," and two clans live
peaceably among the mutants of the Achilles Republic.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'blood-rider');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'blood-rider';

